ill points to a lot meaning you won't  be able to acquire everything in the  skill tree and even if you do invest  heavily in a particular skill that may  dictate what other skills you should  choose due to skill synergies  resurrected features a respect system so  you aren't entirely locked into the  choices you make but there are  limitations on it so don't plan on being  able to freely experiment at the same  degree that you can in diablo 3.  one gameplay mechanic that might catch  you off guard is stamina essentially you  can only sprint for a limited period of  time before running out of stamina and  being forced to walk you can toggle  between running and walking on your own  to preserve stamina and ensure you  aren't left on empty if you suddenly  need to put some distance between you  and an enemy while some items like  stamina potions can help provide a boost  is still something you should always  keep an eye on along with your health  and mana particularly if you're playing  solo  the first time you die you might be  surprised to find that you'll respawn  back in town  sans gear in order to recover your loot  you'll need to make your way back to  your corpse and pick it up  but  without any armor you'll be extremely  vulnerable so keeping backup items in  your stash for these cases is a smart  move though be aware that you'll need a  room in your inventory to pick up your  previous items if you're venturing into  a tough fight it's also wise to open a  town portal before starting which will  save you the frustrating walk all the  way back to where you died  luckily if you do die again before  recovering your corpse you'll just drop  additional corpses so this isn't a case  where you only have a single chance to  get your gear back you can also save  yourself some potential headache by  storing gold in your stash ensuring you  won't need to recover your corpse to get  it back of course if you're playing on  hardcore mode where single death spells  to end all of your progress is lost upon  death but at least you won't need to  store pesky backup armor right  be mindful of fights with enemies who  can resurrect their allies and when you  can always tackle them first they're not  just respawning hordes of enemies on  repeat definitely pay attention to the  enemy attributes displayed at the top of  the screen where you might see a stat  raises fallen showing that this will be  an enemy who can use resurrection  throughout the game you'll encounter  other enemies that should be prioritized  ahead of lesser foes  among the items available from the npc  acara your first quest giver are two  tomes one for scrolls of town portal and  another for scrolls of identify these  scrolls are highly useful as the former  let you quickly visit town and then  return to the action while the latter  reveal hidden attributes on items which  must be done before they're equipped  you'll always want to have some of these  scrolls on you even though they do take  up some inventory space  that said each of these can hold up to  20 of their respective scrolls so they  are definitely worth the space  investment once you enlist the help of  deckard kane the need for scrolls have  identified will be dramatically reduced  and he'll be able to identify items and  mass whenever you return to town but  you'll want access to town portals  throughout the game  you'll come across a lot of loot as you  play and not all of it is necessarily  worth picking up while you can sell  anything back in town repeatedly  returning can quickly become tedious and  will cost you a small amount in the form  of a scroll of town portal  as such your time is better spent only  picking up more valuable items those  that are specific to a class like wands  sacred globes scepters barbarian helmets  and so on are a good bet as are rings  amulets and items that provide a point  to one of a class's skills  focus on nabbing these instead of bolts  or other low value items that take up a  lot of space to maximize your earnings  and reduce the number of trips back to  town you need to make  diablo 2 doesn't have an end game like  you'd expect from a modern game and  eventually you'll likely spend a lot of  time on boss runs where you repeatedly  square off against the boss to earn  better items  but even before reaching that point you  may find yourself underpowered so you'll  want to grind out xp and items by  repeating certain sections of the game  tristam the countess act 1's catacombs  act 2's tombs act 3's council and so on  are fertile ground for earning xp more  quickly than usual so be prepared to  make your way through these numerous  times  everyone can enlist help even without  diving into multiplayer as you progress  through the early act 1 story you'll  gain the ability to hire your first  mercenary from kasia you can only have  one merc at a time so you want to make  sure you choose one that complements  your class  pay attention to their skills when  looking to hire one a rogue with cold  arrow might be less useful to you if  you're a sorceress who can already slow  down enemies or a necromancer with  summons who will divert enemies  attention once you have a mercenary make  sure to equip them with gear to increase  their effectiveness also of note is that  ethereal items which can't be repaired  are useful with mercs due to the fact  that merc equipped items don't lose  durability  [Music]  early on you'll begin acquiring gems  that can be placed into items with  sockets these can be extremely  beneficial and socketed weapons in  particular can provide you with a major  damage boost even if the inherent  attributes of an item aren't great bear  in mind that a sufficient number of  sockets can be transformative if you use  them in the right way  and that's where room words come in like  the various gems you'll find runes can  be placed into sockets for beneficial  effects but if specific runes are  inserted into items in a particular  order you'll activate a rune word which  provides extremely important effects  that go beyond what the individual runes  would normally provide this allows you  to even be able to use abilities for  classes that wouldn't normally have them  you can find rumored lists online from  the original game but a crucial thing to  note is that they're only compatible  with items that have gray text  for example magical items which are  designated by their blue text don't  support rune words all of that said the  stats of the item are still relevant for  making the most of a room word so don't  be too quick to throw runes into the  first item with sockets that you happen  upon in the early game farming countess  in act 1 is a good way to acquire runes  in act 2 you'll acquire the haradric  cube by placing specific items inside  the cube can convert them into something  else there are tons of recipes but it's  important to know that even something as  simple as chip gems can be placed inside  to upgrade them to the next level of  rarity three chipped rubies become one  flawed ruby while three flawed rubies  become one ruby and so on three runes of  the same type can also be combined to  obtain a different specific rune or an  equippable item can be upgraded to the  next rarity level  [Music]  so these are all of our beginner tips  for you if you're new to diablo 2. and  if this is your first time playing get  ready for one of gaming's classics and a  game that would go on to be hugely  influential in the industry if you  enjoyed this video make sure to hit that  like and subscribe button and let us  know what you think of diablo 2  resurrected  oh  okay

